# Unity test execution

Do **not** run Unity Test Framework suites from the agent via:

- Unity Editor CLI / batchmode (`Unity.exe -runTests`, `-batchmode`, etc.)
- External shells, scripts, or CI wrappers invoked from the agent to drive those runs
- Waiting on / polling outside Unity processes for Edit Mode or Play Mode results

CLI and outside-process Unity test runs are unreliable in this environment (project
locks, early process exit, incomplete logs).

## Prefer

- Write or update UTF Edit Mode / Play Mode tests in the package
- Ask the user to run the relevant suites inside the open Unity Editor
- Use code review and static reasoning when verifying behavior without Editor results

## Still allowed

- Non-Unity commands (git, file search, builds that are not Unity test batchmode)
- Reading existing test result / log files the user already produced
